## Key Learnings
1. In Pekko `RetrySupport.retry` treats a delay function returning None as an immediate retry, never as a stop signal, and RetrySpec lines 120-140 observes it.
2. Pekko `FutureTimeoutSupport.timeoutCompletionStage` cancels the CompletableFuture on timeout, while `timeout` has only a branch guarded by an isInstanceOf CompletableFuture check, so a no-cancel acceptance criterion needs that distinction.
3. Pekko circuit breaker call listeners can fire both failure and success for one call when a custom failure function classifies a failed future as non-failure.
4. The serialize-messages check has real actor-tests specs (SerializeSpec, DispatchSpec, FunctionRefSpec), contradicting the earlier claim that none exists.
5. DeadLetterListener resumes logging lazily on the next dead letter after the deadline using Deadline.now, with no scheduler, so a scheduler dependency edge is wrong.
